WEBVTT

00:11.306 --> 00:14.273
Okay, who'd like to start
us off with show-and-tell?

00:14.308 --> 00:15.940
Stewie?

00:15.975 --> 00:18.975
Yes, today I brought in
my mother's driver's license.

00:19.011 --> 00:21.911
Now, if you look closely,
she's clearly drunk.

00:21.946 --> 00:23.711
You could put a Breathalyzer up
to that photo

00:23.747 --> 00:25.445
and she'd get a DUI.

00:25.481 --> 00:27.613
Ha-ha, Stewie's naked!

00:27.649 --> 00:29.148
What?!

00:31.118 --> 00:32.550
Oh, my God!
Don't look! Don't look!

00:32.585 --> 00:34.351
Cell phones down!
Cell phones down!

00:40.590 --> 00:43.290
What the deuce?!
Stewie!

00:43.325 --> 00:44.957
Run from the monster.

00:44.992 --> 00:47.326
You might have to drive.

00:52.331 --> 00:55.096
Thank you all so much
for coming this evening

00:55.132 --> 00:57.598
to my very fancy dinner party.

00:57.633 --> 01:00.500
Oh, my God!
I'm at Glenn Close's house!

01:00.535 --> 01:02.601
You look very handsome tonight,
Stewie.

01:02.636 --> 01:04.269
Well, thank you.
And you're the prettiest

01:04.305 --> 01:06.804
of all the women I know
whose name is Glenn.

01:06.840 --> 01:08.805
Everyone,
please finish your salads,

01:08.841 --> 01:11.073
because our main course tonight
is...

01:11.108 --> 01:13.908
boiled rabbit.

01:15.444 --> 01:17.343
I-I don't... I don't get that.

01:17.378 --> 01:19.612
It seems weird that I'd have
a joke in my own dream

01:19.647 --> 01:21.580
that I don't get.
Oh, thank you so...

01:29.753 --> 01:31.319
Quick, you're
almost on!

01:31.354 --> 01:32.519
What? I'm on?

01:32.554 --> 01:34.554
But I don't know any
of my lines!

01:40.125 --> 01:41.892
♪ It seems today ♪

01:41.927 --> 01:43.893
♪ That all you see ♪

01:43.928 --> 01:47.294
♪ Is violence in
movies and sex on TV ♪

01:47.330 --> 01:50.630
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

01:50.665 --> 01:53.832
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪
(mumbling gibberish)

01:53.868 --> 01:57.168
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

01:57.203 --> 02:00.836
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

02:00.872 --> 02:02.437
♪ All the things that make us ♪
(mumbling gibberish)

02:02.472 --> 02:04.439
♪ Pumpkin pie ♪

02:04.474 --> 02:06.106
What the hell? Put
him on the bench.

02:06.141 --> 02:08.507
Wait, please, no!
I just wasn't ready!

02:08.543 --> 02:11.376
Don't worry.
We'll put you in soon.

02:11.411 --> 02:12.576
Ho-ho-ho!

02:12.612 --> 02:15.612
Is funny
because you won't be back!

02:15.647 --> 02:16.117
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

02:23.685 --> 02:26.051
Wait, how did Joe get halfway up
those stairs?

02:26.087 --> 02:27.218
Lois, get in here!

02:27.254 --> 02:29.087
It's dark and I'm frightened!

02:32.223 --> 02:34.223
I think they've got this thing
backwards.

02:35.859 --> 02:37.491
Hey, wake up!

02:37.526 --> 02:40.693
I had a bad dream, so now
your night has to be terrible.

02:40.729 --> 02:42.160
Peter, Stewie's upset.

02:42.196 --> 02:44.162
Scooch over so he
can sleep with us.

02:44.198 --> 02:45.963
Oh, come on.
Are you serious?

02:45.999 --> 02:47.631
Last time, he kicked me
all night.

02:47.666 --> 02:50.466
And I got a big day tomorrow.
I got two shows.

02:50.501 --> 02:52.467
All right, folks,
big treat for you today.

02:52.502 --> 02:54.068
He's a little shy.

02:54.104 --> 02:56.737
Put your hands together
for Sham-Peter!

02:56.772 --> 02:59.738
I'm not shy! I'm angry!

02:59.773 --> 03:02.473
I'm in constant pain!

03:02.508 --> 03:05.642
This act has been condemned
by over 30 nations!

03:05.677 --> 03:08.543
I'm gonna kill you all!

03:12.214 --> 03:14.180
<i>Ah, crap.
I can't sleep like this.</i>

03:14.216 --> 03:15.848
<i>And now my mind is racin'.</i>

03:15.883 --> 03:18.116
<i>Like, how does that candle
in Beauty and the Beast</i>

03:18.151 --> 03:20.317
<i>sing so good?
I mean, the teapot I get,</i>

03:20.352 --> 03:22.852
<i>'cause she's a girl. But
the candle, I don't under...</i>

03:22.887 --> 03:24.519
<i>Oh, he's French. That's why.</i>

03:29.724 --> 03:31.157
Couch it is, I guess.

03:31.192 --> 03:32.958
Oh, my God. The couch is gone.

03:32.993 --> 03:34.492
Where the hell is...
Oh, that's right.

03:34.527 --> 03:36.527
Couchella is this weekend.

03:38.130 --> 03:40.229
Hey, man,
where you been?!

03:40.264 --> 03:43.231
I just had sex with
a girl on her period!

03:43.266 --> 03:45.832
Dude, that's not a brag!

03:50.404 --> 03:52.369
So, how fat are you?

03:52.405 --> 03:54.871
240? Nice.

03:54.906 --> 03:56.872
Oh, Peter! What are
you doing down here?

03:56.907 --> 03:59.373
Oh, hey, Brian. Stewie
kind of took over our bed,

03:59.409 --> 04:00.908
so I'm looking
for a place to sleep.

04:00.944 --> 04:02.309
Well, why don't you
go up to the attic?

04:02.344 --> 04:03.910
I think there's even
a futon up there.

04:03.946 --> 04:05.511
Huh. That's a great idea.

04:05.546 --> 04:07.178
Geez, I'm glad you came along.

04:07.213 --> 04:10.113
I'm gonna sleep better
than a cartoon sheriff.

04:19.354 --> 04:22.654
I was in jail 'cause
I killed a bunch of old ladies.

04:22.690 --> 04:25.389
And now that I'm out,
I'm gonna do it again.

04:33.296 --> 04:35.395
Wow, Stewie,
you look exhausted.

04:35.431 --> 04:38.397
Yeah, 'cause I was up super late
last night, beefing your mom.

04:38.433 --> 04:39.261
My mom's dead.

04:39.285 --> 04:40.900
Yeah, 'cause I
beefed her to death.

04:40.901 --> 04:43.701
Whoa, what's your problem?
Why are you being such a jerk?

04:43.736 --> 04:46.169
I'm sorry, Brian.
I had the absolute worst night.

04:46.204 --> 04:49.370
I had a weird dream.
A frightening dream.

04:49.405 --> 04:50.871
Yeah, Stewie,
that's called a nightmare.

04:50.907 --> 04:52.872
Sounds like you must've had
your first one.

04:52.908 --> 04:54.406
That's what a
nightmare is?

04:54.442 --> 04:56.608
I thought "nightmare"
meant, like, being invited

04:56.643 --> 04:58.009
to an apartment party.

04:58.044 --> 04:59.876
Get a house if you
want to have a party.

04:59.912 --> 05:01.545
I'm not going to a
party in an apartment.

05:01.580 --> 05:02.712
Relax, it's no big deal.

05:02.747 --> 05:04.312
People have nightmares
all the time.

05:04.348 --> 05:07.114
Oh, no, Brian. I am not living
through that horror again.

05:07.149 --> 05:09.615
In fact, I've decided
that from this day forward,

05:09.651 --> 05:12.417
I shall never allow myself
to fall asleep again.

05:12.453 --> 05:13.418
Come on, that's ridiculous.

05:13.454 --> 05:14.618
How do you think
you're gonna do that?

05:14.654 --> 05:16.153
I don't know.
Maybe I'll get a job

05:16.189 --> 05:18.588
working the night
shift at a supermarket.

05:18.623 --> 05:20.255
Hey, where's
the vegetable aisle?

05:20.291 --> 05:23.558
Yeah, right, it's 2:00 a.m.
You're not here for vegetables.

05:23.593 --> 05:26.493
Well, I got the
12 cucumbers.

05:26.528 --> 05:28.361
What's wrong?
Just this guy at the...

05:28.396 --> 05:30.261
Never mind.

05:34.165 --> 05:35.732
Peter, we have a hamper.

05:35.767 --> 05:38.667
Stop throwing your dirty clothes
in the toilet.

05:38.702 --> 05:39.834
Peter?

05:39.869 --> 05:41.701
Peter, where are you?

05:44.839 --> 05:46.804
What's all this?

05:46.840 --> 05:49.272
Oh, hey, Lois.
Welcome to the Pete Pad,

05:49.308 --> 05:52.208
where the dancing's hot,
the drinks are hot...

05:52.243 --> 05:53.743
Everything's
just freakin' hot.

05:53.778 --> 05:55.610
What have you
done to the attic?

05:55.645 --> 05:56.877
Well, when I slept up here
the other night,

05:56.912 --> 05:58.479
I realized
what a great space it is.

05:58.514 --> 06:01.280
So I dragged up some stuff and
turned it into a sweet hangout.

06:01.316 --> 06:04.615
Even made it extra awesome
by stealing a real street sign.

06:08.286 --> 06:10.319
I don't understand. What
are you gonna do up here?

06:10.354 --> 06:12.253
Eh, mostly just burn the roof
of my mouth

06:12.288 --> 06:14.588
on unevenly-heated
microwave burritos.

06:14.623 --> 06:17.590
Now I'm busy, so close the floor
and get out of here.

06:23.029 --> 06:24.660
All right, all right,
come on, Stewie.

06:24.696 --> 06:26.995
You've got to stay awake.
I know what'll help.

06:27.031 --> 06:28.330
I'll watch that preview channel

06:28.365 --> 06:30.498
that always has
inconsistent volumes.

06:30.533 --> 06:33.433
<i>They're mother and daughter
but also best friends.</i>

06:33.468 --> 06:36.334
<i>Catch Gilmore Girls
on Channel 367.</i>

06:36.369 --> 06:39.368
<i>You can name your own price
for hotel rooms!</i>

06:53.580 --> 06:55.479
Help! Please!

06:56.748 --> 06:59.915
Damn it! Why can't I move?!

07:05.187 --> 07:06.352
Aah!

07:06.387 --> 07:08.054
Stewie, you okay?
What happened?

07:08.089 --> 07:09.754
I was just sitting here
on the couch and I had

07:09.790 --> 07:11.455
another nightmare
about that horrible monster.

07:11.490 --> 07:12.823
Okay, that's it.

07:12.858 --> 07:14.991
I'm gonna help you get these
nightmares under control.

07:15.026 --> 07:16.925
Really?
Oh, thank you, Brian.

07:16.960 --> 07:19.460
And maybe I can help you
control your strange obsession

07:19.495 --> 07:20.861
with eating
pencil erasers.

07:20.897 --> 07:23.263
It's not an obsession.

07:23.298 --> 07:24.797
Mmm, mmm, oh, yeah.

07:24.832 --> 07:26.497
Oh, so rubbery. Mmm.

07:26.533 --> 07:28.665
It's like a little
steak. Mmm, mmm.

07:28.700 --> 07:29.966
Brian, you really should...

07:30.002 --> 07:32.068
The world is small and
safe when I do this!

07:38.477 --> 07:40.996
Okay, Stewie, I read the review
of a dream book on Amazon,

07:41.031 --> 07:42.430
so I think I can help you.

07:42.465 --> 07:45.699
Literally every other tab
is open to Lusty Matures.

07:45.734 --> 07:47.266
Yup, that's what
it takes now.

07:47.301 --> 07:49.233
Anyway, it says here
that most nightmares

07:49.269 --> 07:51.168
are born of
subconscious fears.

07:51.203 --> 07:52.869
So maybe if we make
a list of the things

07:52.905 --> 07:55.004
you're most afraid of,
we can face and conquer

07:55.039 --> 07:56.871
these fears together, and
then your nightmares'll end.

07:56.907 --> 07:59.039
Huh, that's actually
a good idea.

07:59.075 --> 08:01.240
Like the U.S. Army Reserves.

08:02.744 --> 08:05.410
We're completely surrounded.
We need reinforcements.

08:05.446 --> 08:07.611
You know who could
really bail us out?

08:07.647 --> 08:11.447
Somebody who works five days
a week at Enterprise Rent-A-Car.

08:15.485 --> 08:17.951
These new digs of yours
are pretty great, Peter.

08:17.987 --> 08:20.353
Hey, I brought
construction paper and markers

08:20.388 --> 08:22.320
in case you guys
want to draw breasts.

08:22.356 --> 08:26.089
Cool. But before that, who's up
for another insulation fight?

08:26.124 --> 08:27.857
I'm in.
Heck yeah.

08:30.227 --> 08:31.792
Ha!

08:31.828 --> 08:33.827
Gotcha!

08:36.263 --> 08:37.429
Missed me.

08:37.465 --> 08:39.297
Sneak attack!

08:45.803 --> 08:47.402
What are you
doing up here?

08:47.437 --> 08:49.336
I need you to take
the trash out.

08:49.372 --> 08:50.604
You know what?
I'm gonna use this

08:50.639 --> 08:52.972
Peter Doesn't Have to Take Out
the Trash coupon

08:53.008 --> 08:54.139
that I got for my anniversary.

08:54.174 --> 08:55.841
You gave that to yourself.

08:55.875 --> 08:57.808
I don't know,
it says "official."

08:57.844 --> 08:59.542
Oh, forget it,
I'll do it myself.

08:59.578 --> 09:02.511
This whole attic
business is ridiculous.

09:02.546 --> 09:04.512
Hey, guys, check it out.

09:04.547 --> 09:06.613
I'm a lady.

09:06.648 --> 09:07.948
Joe...

09:07.983 --> 09:10.449
you hit a home run with
that, I want to try it.

09:14.487 --> 09:16.686
All right, Stewie,
time to tackle your fears.

09:16.721 --> 09:18.887
Now, it sounds like
you're scared of monsters.

09:18.922 --> 09:21.389
So to help you get over it.
here's Frankenstein.

09:21.424 --> 09:24.391
I'm Frankenstein.

09:24.426 --> 09:26.091
I'm actually really nice.

09:26.127 --> 09:29.127
There's no need
to be scared of me.

09:29.162 --> 09:30.395
Seriously?

09:30.430 --> 09:32.362
This is obviously
Chris in a costume.

09:32.398 --> 09:34.296
Huh. Well, that
can't be possible.

09:34.332 --> 09:36.965
Because here comes Chris
walking in the door right now.

09:37.000 --> 09:39.533
Hey, hey, hey.
Here comes Chris Griffin,

09:39.568 --> 09:40.833
a-roodly-toot-toot.

09:40.869 --> 09:42.201
Yeah, okay,
whatever, Meg.

09:42.237 --> 09:43.435
Meg?

09:43.470 --> 09:45.303
You must be
talking about me,

09:45.339 --> 09:47.338
a-roodly-toot-toot.

09:55.011 --> 09:56.710
Do they all say
"a-roodly-toot-toot"?

09:56.745 --> 09:58.210
A lot of them, yeah.

10:02.315 --> 10:03.947
Chris, I'm putting
together a load of laundry.

10:03.983 --> 10:05.882
You got anything?

10:07.452 --> 10:09.384
Damn it, Peter.

10:09.420 --> 10:11.886
Are you guys playing lawn darts
in the attic again?

10:11.921 --> 10:13.253
No.

10:13.288 --> 10:14.521
Yay, lawn darts!

10:14.556 --> 10:15.921
Peter wins lawn darts.

10:15.956 --> 10:17.656
She's dumb.
She got no idea.

10:20.692 --> 10:22.025
All right, Peter,
that's enough.

10:22.061 --> 10:23.592
It is time to
get out of...

10:23.628 --> 10:25.061
What the hell?

10:25.096 --> 10:27.762
Oh, yeah, we put Joe
in Stewie's old Jolly Jumper.

10:27.798 --> 10:30.097
You told me this was
a paratrooper's harness.

10:30.132 --> 10:31.831
Shut up, baby man.

10:31.866 --> 10:33.432
That's it. This
is our home,

10:33.467 --> 10:35.467
not some frat house for
you and your friends.

10:35.502 --> 10:37.802
Now, I want you out
of this attic now.

10:37.837 --> 10:39.035
No way, we ain't leaving.

10:39.071 --> 10:40.503
We're having
too much fun up here.

10:40.538 --> 10:42.805
Quagmire just showed us
his Eric McCormack impression.

10:42.840 --> 10:44.505
There could be
no such thing.

10:44.541 --> 10:46.106
Well, that's what I said,
but then he did it,

10:46.141 --> 10:48.407
and I was like, "Oh, all right,
okay, yeah, kind of."

10:48.443 --> 10:50.675
Fine. You like the
damn attic so much?

10:50.710 --> 10:52.544
Then enjoy the attic!

10:57.482 --> 10:59.314
Did... did she just
lock us in here?

10:59.349 --> 11:00.714
It looks like it.

11:00.750 --> 11:04.484
Guys, spin me back.
I didn't see what happened.

11:08.054 --> 11:10.654
So, how'd it go last night?
Did we cure your nightmares?

11:10.689 --> 11:12.856
No, not at all. They
were worse than ever.

11:12.891 --> 11:14.857
Which is why I built this.

11:23.330 --> 11:24.729
What the hell is that?

11:24.765 --> 11:26.797
It's a Digital Dream Interface.

11:26.833 --> 11:28.565
You see, once connected
to this device,

11:28.600 --> 11:31.433
you will be able to enter
my sleeping mind, where

11:31.469 --> 11:33.508
you will end these horrible
dreams once and for all.

11:33.536 --> 11:34.869
I'm gonna do what?

11:36.205 --> 11:37.471
What... what-what
does he want?

11:37.506 --> 11:38.704
What is he saying?

11:38.739 --> 11:40.172
I think he's saying
"a-roodly-toot-toot".

11:40.208 --> 11:42.507
We just can't understand him
because of the way he talks.

11:43.809 --> 11:46.075
Oh, no, no, I think
he just needs a ride home.

11:50.196 --> 11:51.561
Stewie, you can't be serious.

11:51.597 --> 11:53.028
Oh, I'm very serious.

11:53.064 --> 11:55.396
You and I will place these
cranial impulse receptor caps

11:55.432 --> 11:57.198
on our heads, I shall
begin my slumber, and...

11:57.234 --> 11:58.873
And then this thing
will actually allow me

11:58.901 --> 12:00.067
to enter your dream?

12:00.102 --> 12:01.334
That's right, Brian.

12:01.369 --> 12:03.401
I want you to come inside
me while I'm asleep.

12:03.437 --> 12:04.836
Do-Don't... don't
say it like that.

12:04.871 --> 12:07.104
And once you're in my
dream, your job is to stop

12:07.139 --> 12:09.539
these nightmares by finding
that monster and killing him.

12:09.574 --> 12:11.406
This isn't a job
for the meek, Brian.

12:11.442 --> 12:13.474
When you get in there,
you've got to be hard.

12:13.509 --> 12:14.942
Okay, but that
felt intentional.

12:14.978 --> 12:16.343
All right,
let's get to it.

12:17.546 --> 12:18.936
This is your receptor cap.

12:18.971 --> 12:20.511
Over here is your REM monitor.

12:20.547 --> 12:21.713
What's this thing do?

12:21.748 --> 12:23.680
Oh, that's just a little
bike bell for fun.

12:23.716 --> 12:25.615
I found it at the crosswalk

12:25.650 --> 12:27.250
where those kids
got creamed the other day.

12:27.285 --> 12:28.483
Anyway, let's get started.

12:57.736 --> 13:00.202
Hello? Stewie?

13:10.410 --> 13:13.010
Ah, you must be
Brian. I'm Glenn.

13:13.045 --> 13:16.512
<i>Yes, I know. You were
very mean in 101 Dalmations.</i>

13:16.547 --> 13:19.748
Thank you. Would you like
to do the Bristol Stomp?

13:19.783 --> 13:21.815
♪ The kids in Bristol
are sharp as a pistol ♪

13:21.851 --> 13:24.250
♪ When they do
the Bristol Stomp ♪

13:24.286 --> 13:25.528
How does he even know this?

13:25.529 --> 13:25.953
♪ Really somethin' when
they join in jumpin' ♪

13:25.954 --> 13:28.360
He heard it once in the car.

13:30.722 --> 13:32.955
Jeez, Lois
is really serious.

13:32.990 --> 13:34.989
I can't believe
she left us up here all night.

13:35.025 --> 13:36.658
Damn it, we got to do something.

13:36.693 --> 13:39.059
Maybe if we just scream for help
someone'll hear us.

13:39.094 --> 13:42.361
Help! Help! Help!

13:42.397 --> 13:44.029
In case of a bear attack,
you should

13:44.064 --> 13:45.663
A, lie down,

13:45.698 --> 13:47.430
B, run downhill,

13:47.465 --> 13:49.898
or C, stand your ground?

13:58.172 --> 14:00.138
...and just because
of the roles I play,

14:00.173 --> 14:03.473
people always assume
I'm very serious in real life.

14:03.509 --> 14:05.374
Yeah, I could see that.
But I'm not.

14:05.410 --> 14:07.776
I'm very capable
of being silly, too.

14:07.811 --> 14:10.077
See, watch, I'll show you.

14:10.112 --> 14:12.345
Fart.

14:12.380 --> 14:15.614
I, uh... Did-did...
did you just say "fart"?

14:15.649 --> 14:18.249
Yes, that's me
being rather silly.

14:18.284 --> 14:19.684
Well, hello, Brian.

14:19.719 --> 14:21.351
I say, what
brings you here?

14:21.386 --> 14:23.819
Stewie, hey! I'm here
to find and kill the monster

14:23.854 --> 14:25.286
that's been causing
all your nightmares.

14:25.322 --> 14:26.921
Oh, that sounds
wonderful! Let's do it!

14:26.956 --> 14:28.188
Oh, but real quick,

14:28.223 --> 14:30.323
I'm just gonna turn
into Elmo for a second.

14:30.358 --> 14:31.791
Hi, Brian!

14:31.826 --> 14:34.792
Elmo speak bad English
on educational show!

14:34.827 --> 14:36.560
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha!

14:36.595 --> 14:38.594
Okay, I'm back.
Let's go.

14:40.164 --> 14:42.030
This way to the
subconscious.

14:49.736 --> 14:52.003
Oh, this seems rather pleasant.
Yeah.

14:52.038 --> 14:54.504
Hey, you know, that Glenn Close
salad actually wasn't bad.

14:54.540 --> 14:57.073
Yeah, a lot of my dreams
have pretty good salad.

14:58.975 --> 15:01.375
Oh, no.
What?! Where are we?!

15:01.410 --> 15:02.775
We're at the doctor!

15:02.811 --> 15:05.677
Time for a baby shot
in your fanny!

15:27.959 --> 15:31.760
Come give Grandpa a sloppy,
old-man, coffee kiss!

15:51.006 --> 15:53.940
Would you like some candy?

15:53.975 --> 15:56.641
Help me find my lost puppy?

15:56.677 --> 15:59.377
I like your mouth and butt.

16:01.179 --> 16:02.644
What the hell was that?!

16:02.680 --> 16:04.846
Lois has painted a very
dark picture of abduction.

16:06.349 --> 16:09.216
Adult stuff,
adult stuff, adult stuff.

16:09.251 --> 16:12.217
The world is scary,
adult stuff, adult stuff.

16:12.252 --> 16:15.853
Scary people yelling in another
part of the world, adult stuff.

16:17.188 --> 16:19.621
I wish Mom wouldn't watch
the news in front of me!

16:19.656 --> 16:21.757
Coming up: a map with
a hurricane on it.

16:21.792 --> 16:24.958
And you don't know
your states yet!

16:32.064 --> 16:35.331
Aah! That one trip to the
petting zoo really messed me up!

16:35.366 --> 16:36.998
I saw too much!

16:52.576 --> 16:54.675
Stewie, look!

16:55.912 --> 16:57.977
It's the monster!

16:58.013 --> 16:59.544
Quick, Brian!
Kill it!

16:59.580 --> 17:00.846
Oh, there you guys are.

17:00.881 --> 17:02.246
I would've been here sooner,

17:02.282 --> 17:05.315
but one of my legs is a snake
that's very hungry for mice.

17:33.734 --> 17:36.167
Nice shot.
Get it? Shot?

17:36.202 --> 17:37.668
<i>All right, bye!</i>

17:40.672 --> 17:42.304
You did it, Brian!

17:42.339 --> 17:44.405
You killed
the monster!

17:47.909 --> 17:49.608
What the hell?!

17:49.643 --> 17:50.943
It's me!

17:50.978 --> 17:52.710
Oh, my God,
you're right!

17:52.745 --> 17:54.611
But I... I don't understand.

17:54.646 --> 17:56.712
<i>Why am I the source
of your fears?</i>

17:56.747 --> 17:58.414
Huh. I'm
not sure.

17:58.449 --> 18:00.815
Maybe this means
that deep down,

18:00.850 --> 18:04.250
the thing I'm most afraid
of is disappointing you.

18:04.285 --> 18:07.252
Me? Wh-Why do you care so much
about what I think?

18:07.287 --> 18:08.486
Well, think about it.

18:08.522 --> 18:10.387
You've been more of a
father figure to me

18:10.423 --> 18:12.655
than the fat man ever
has been or ever will be.

18:12.691 --> 18:14.656
Look, I know
I'm always busting your balls,

18:14.692 --> 18:17.358
but it's just because you're
the only person in this house

18:17.393 --> 18:19.426
whose judgment
actually matters to me.

18:19.461 --> 18:22.161
Wow. Thanks, Stewie.

18:22.196 --> 18:25.029
But listen, you-you never have
to worry about letting me down.

18:25.065 --> 18:26.663
I'll always be proud of you.

18:26.699 --> 18:28.732
In fact, I already am.

18:28.767 --> 18:29.665
You are?

18:29.701 --> 18:30.833
'Course I am.

18:30.868 --> 18:32.634
I mean, you're only a baby,
and yet,

18:32.669 --> 18:34.668
you're one of the most
amazing people I know.

18:34.704 --> 18:36.869
Well, thank you, Brian.

18:39.006 --> 18:41.173
Well, Stewie, seems like
my work here is done.

18:41.208 --> 18:42.974
What's the best way
out of here?

18:43.009 --> 18:44.741
Oh, yeah, no, that
one stays locked

18:44.776 --> 18:46.109
until the overnight to Vegas

18:46.144 --> 18:48.010
with my college
a cappella group.

18:52.381 --> 18:55.748
Peter, I'm going
crazy up here.

18:55.783 --> 18:56.915
We all are!

18:56.950 --> 18:59.049
You got to talk to Lois!

18:59.085 --> 19:00.284
Damn it, you're right.

19:00.319 --> 19:02.251
Lois, let us out of here!

19:02.287 --> 19:04.519
No way! You like it so much?!

19:04.555 --> 19:06.520
Then you can rot up there
with your buddies!

19:06.556 --> 19:07.788
Lois, so help me God,

19:07.824 --> 19:09.656
if you don't let us out
right this second,

19:09.691 --> 19:11.590
I'm gonna take a dump
on your wedding dress!

19:11.625 --> 19:12.891
You wouldn't dare!

19:12.927 --> 19:15.226
Don't test me. I'll do it!
We'll all do it!

19:15.261 --> 19:16.660
Quagmire, pull down
your pants!

19:16.695 --> 19:18.128
What?! I'm not doing that!

19:18.163 --> 19:19.762
You leave my dress alone, Peter!

19:19.797 --> 19:22.998
If it'll get us out of here,
I'll make a doodie on it.

19:23.033 --> 19:24.231
What, are you nuts?!

19:24.266 --> 19:25.866
I've been crowning
for six hours!

19:25.901 --> 19:27.367
Cleveland's pants are off, Lois!

19:27.402 --> 19:29.001
Here come mine!
This is happening!

19:29.036 --> 19:30.936
Lois, they're not bluffing!
Open the door!

19:30.971 --> 19:32.269
I miss Bonnie!

19:32.305 --> 19:33.903
Damn it, Peter,
you hold that in!

19:33.939 --> 19:35.138
I know you can!

19:35.173 --> 19:36.839
You did it on the ferry
to Block Island!

19:36.874 --> 19:38.507
Oh, my God, I'm gonna puke!

19:38.542 --> 19:40.641
That's good! Puke on the dress!
Puke on the dress!

19:40.677 --> 19:42.042
Aah, damn it!

19:44.078 --> 19:46.644
Not all snake bites are lethal.

19:50.516 --> 19:51.748
There! You happy?!

19:51.783 --> 19:54.216
You were too late.
We pooed on the gown.

19:54.251 --> 19:56.317
Ripped a big hole
in your ceiling, too.

19:56.352 --> 19:57.685
I barfed on Peter's ass.

19:57.720 --> 19:59.786
I-I don't know if it got
on the dress or not, Lois,

19:59.821 --> 20:01.320
but I-I am... I am so sorry.

20:01.355 --> 20:03.988
Yeah, this was all
a huge disaster.

20:04.024 --> 20:08.392
Let's just agree that we both
went a bit too far, hmm?

20:08.427 --> 20:10.426
I, uh... I might...

20:10.461 --> 20:13.328
I might need two weeks off
from this friendship.

20:22.001 --> 20:23.567
Stewie, you awake?

20:23.603 --> 20:25.101
Did you have any nightmares?

20:25.137 --> 20:26.468
I don't think so.

20:26.504 --> 20:28.103
Did you get rid of the monster?

20:28.139 --> 20:30.538
Sure did. Turned out
that monster was nothing more

20:30.573 --> 20:31.805
than a manifestation

20:31.840 --> 20:34.306
of your subconscious desire
not to disappoint me.

20:34.342 --> 20:36.341
Apparently, I'm like
a father figure to you.

20:36.376 --> 20:39.676
Okay. Wow. Somebody's
got a big head.

20:39.712 --> 20:43.146
Stewie, I want you to know...
I'm very proud of you.

20:43.181 --> 20:44.580
All right, that's...
that's awkward.

20:44.615 --> 20:46.480
How-how am I supposed
to respond to that?

20:46.516 --> 20:48.681
You are a good person.
Stop complimenting me.

20:48.717 --> 20:51.617
"Oh, I sure hope the dog
approves of who I am."

20:51.652 --> 20:53.918
I'm out of here, weirdo.

20:55.221 --> 20:57.260
There's a wedding dress out here
covered in.

20:57.261 --> 21:58.237
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru